  "evaluation_scope": "0.22.62 ordinary non-biological Harmony PC port. Original TdlgGenerate and TPTableDlg dialogs use native ArkUI controls; original text editing uses a native editable input/textarea with asynchronous dialog completion. The styled editor preserves text editing but explicitly reports that syntax highlighting is unavailable. The Windows 32-bit Kinect/NUI initializer is compiled with its upstream platform guard intact and remains unavailable on Harmony. Host fixtures use recording backends only; full native sources are separately compiled and strictly linked against Harmony. No application page connection, real system window, HAP/ZIP, install, macro, application Python, research calculation, or overall functional-completion claim is made. The original UpdateThread source now uses only the portable app/log API on Harmony and retains the original mainform include in the wx branch; worker execution and application update workflow remain unconnected. The original THtmlImageCell has a Harmony-specific ArkUI image-node path with ImageKit-backed decoding, image-map hit-testing, responsive sizing, and accessible alternative text. THtml, THtmlManager and the original tag translation unit now provide a native static-help renderer for text, common entities, anchors, image resources, and custom rectangle/circle image maps; it uses an injected platform resource provider and never executes script or embedded macros. The wxWidgets source paths remain byte-identical in the desktop branch. CSS layout, interactive INPUT/SNIPPET/INCLUDE/switch expansion, animated GIF, and integration into the current application page remain incomplete and the new UI path has not been device/simulator verified. The original selected-object SetView behavior is now exposed on Harmony for exactly one selected TXBond or TXPlane: it aligns the view normal, centers on the object, and updates visible grid depth. The action is routed through the retained document session and has targeted C++ translation-unit and plain-TypeScript validation only; full ArkTS build, strict relink, and simulator interaction remain pending; original fragment hide/show-only/select actions are wired through the actual renderer selection; ordinary action errors no longer invalidate the presented document session."
}
